  "rationale": "The target is an OR over dbReplica, mailArchive, shareMount and codeRepo, so at least two independent routes must be checked. Route 1: wifiGuest (entry) -> kerberoast -> jumpHost -> mailArchive -> target. Route 2: backupHost is OR-reachable through tokenCache (from internet) and also through browserStore (from exposedApi). backupHost then reaches the target via dbReplica and also via shareMount. Route 1 and Route 2 share no non-foothold step. Within Route 2, backupHost has two independent parents. Blocking any single step therefore leaves at least one route open. Blocking jumpHost or kerberoast still leaves backupHost -> dbReplica/shareMount. Blocking backupHost, tokenCache or browserStore still leaves jumpHost -> mailArchive and jumpHost -> dbReplica. Blocking mailArchive, dbReplica or shareMount individually also leaves another collection step reachable. No single step is a chokepoint."
